{
  "requirement": "The review prompt MUST direct the reviewer not to re-raise the decisions and open choices that the brief lists.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement `requirements.cli.requirements_review_skill.review_prompt.brief` has one obligation. The review prompt MUST direct the reviewer not to re-raise the decisions and open choices that the brief lists. The prompt is static text with no branches or modes.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_review_prompt_does_not_reraise_the_brief]` carries the `{test}` reference. It loads the shipped prompt through `fn[review_prompt]`, which reads `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/references/review-prompt.md`. It then whitespace-collapses the prompt with `fn[collapse]`. It asserts through `fn[assert_text_in_order]` that two phrases appear, the second after the first:\n- \"the decisions already made, and the open choices already noted\"\n- \"Don't re-raise those\"\n\nI read `assert_text_in_order`. It panics if a phrase is missing or out of order. The two phrases tie the \"don't re-raise\" instruction to the brief's decisions and open choices. A prompt that dropped the instruction, or no longer pointed it at the brief's decisions and open choices, would fail the test. The prompt's actual text matches: \"...the decisions already made, and the open choices already noted. Don't re-raise those.\" The test covers the whole obligation. I found no gaps.",
